gents-harness-comparison-chart=harness-index\",\n       \"h3\": \"Token Usage per Task\",\n       \"caption\": \"Average input, cache, and output tokens per task\",\n       \"accTitle\": \"Input Tokens\",\n       \"notes\": [\n        \"Non-cached input tokens sent to the model, including prompts, instructions, tool context, and task context that were not served from prompt cache.\"\n       ],\n       \"viewBox\": null,\n       \"kinds\": null,\n       \"tables\": 0\n      },\n      {\n       \"tab\": \"Token Distribution\",\n       \"param\": \"?coding-agents-token-usage-chart=token-distribution&coding-agents-performance-chart=index&coding-agents-harness-comparison-chart=harness-index\",\n       \"h3\": \"Token Usage Distribution\",\n       \"caption\": \"Spread of total tokens per task (P5, P25, P50, P75, P95)\",\n       \"accTitle\": \"What This Chart Shows\",\n       \"notes\": [\n        \"This box plot shows the spread of total token usage per task for each agent across the benchmark suite, using observed percentiles (P5, P25, P50, P75, P95) of per-task total tokens.\"\n       ],\n       \"viewBox\": null,\n       \"kinds\": null,\n       \"tables\": 0\n      },\n      {\n       \"tab\": \"Cache Hit Rate\",\n       \"param\": \"?coding-agents-token-usage-chart=cache-efficiency&coding-agents-performance-chart=index&coding-agents-harness-comparison-chart=harness-index\",\n       \"h3\": \"Cache Hit Rate\",\n       \"caption\": \"Average cache hit rate per task · Higher is better\",\n       \"accTitle\": \"What Cache Hit Rate Shows\",\n       \"notes\": [\n        \"This chart shows the average cache hit rate exposed by the benchmark view for each agent. Higher values indicate a larger share of requests or prompt reuse being served from provider-side cache rather than treated as a fully fresh input, which can reduce effective token cost when those discounts are available.\"\n       ],\n       \"viewBox\": null,\n       \"kinds\": null,\n       \"tables\": 0\n      },\n      {\n       \"tab\": \"Input vs. Output\",\n       \"param\": \"?coding-agents-token-usage-chart=input-vs-output-tokens&coding-agents-performance-chart=index&coding-agents-harness-comparison-chart=harness-index\",\n       \"h3\": \"Input vs. Output Token Usage\",\n       \"caption\": \"Average input tokens vs. average output tokens per task\",\n       \"accTitle\": \"What This Chart Shows\",\n       \"notes\": [\n        \"This chart compares how much context an agent consumes with how much text it emits. It is a useful way to spot agents that are especially input-heavy, output-heavy, or balanced in their token usage.\"\n       ],\n       \"viewBox\": null,\n       \"kinds\": null,\n       \"tables\": 0\n      },\n      {\n       \"tab\": \"Tokens by Benchmark\",\n       \"param\": \"?coding-agents-token-usage-chart=tokens-by-benchmark&coding-agents-performance-chart=index&coding-agents-harness-comparison-chart=harness-index\",\n       \"h3\": \"Tokens by Benchmark\",\n       \"caption\": \"Average token usage on each component benchmark\",\n       \"accTitle\": \"How to Read This Chart\",\n       \"notes\": [\n        \"This chart breaks token usage out by benchmark component so you can compare how expensive an agent is on different task families. The values here use the per-eval input and output token telemetry currently exposed in the benchmark view.\"\n       ],\n       \"viewBox\": null,\n       \"kinds\": null,\n       \"tables\": 0\n      }\n     ]\n    },\n    {\n     \"tabs\": null,\n     \"panels\": [\n      {\n       \"h3\": \"Artificial Analysis Coding Agent Index vs. Total Tokens\",\n       \"caption\": \"Artificial Analysis Coding Agent Index vs. average total tokens per task\",\n       \"accTitle\": \"How to Read This Chart\",\n       \"notes\": [\n        \"Each point represents a coding-agent variant. Farther right means higher benchmark performance, while lower token usage appears farther left. Agents toward the upper-left use fewer token