, P95) (USD)\",\n       \"accTitle\": \"What This Chart Shows\",\n       \"notes\": [\n        \"This box plot shows the spread of cost per task for each agent across the benchmark suite, using observed percentiles (P5, P25, P50, P75, P95) of per-task cost.\"\n       ],\n       \"viewBox\": null,\n       \"kinds\": null,\n       \"tables\": 0\n      },\n      {\n       \"tab\": \"Total Cost\",\n       \"param\": \"?coding-agents-token-usage-chart=token-usage&coding-agents-performance-chart=index&coding-agents-harness-comparison-chart=harness-index&coding-agents-cost-chart=total-cost\",\n       \"h3\": \"Total Cost Across the Artificial Analysis Coding Agent Index\",\n       \"caption\": \"Total pay-per-token API cost across all benchmark tasks (USD) · Lower is better\",\n       \"accTitle\": \"What Total Cost Is Measuring\",\n       \"notes\": [\n        \"This chart shows the summed pay-per-token API cost across all tasks included in the selected Artificial Analysis Coding Agent Index, expressed in USD and based on provider token pricing.\",\n        \"It uses the benchmark row view's aggregated cost totals, so it reflects the overall API spend required to run the benchmark tasks for that agent configuration, including cached-input discounts and cache-write charges where applicable, not the average cost of a single task.\"\n       ],\n       \"viewBox\": null,\n       \"kinds\": null,\n       \"tables\": 0\n      }\n     ]\n    },\n    {\n     \"tabs\": null,\n     \"panels\": [\n      {\n       \"h3\": \"Artificial Analysis Coding Agent Index vs. Cost per Task\",\n       \"caption\": \"Artificial Analysis Coding Agent Index vs. average pay-per-token API cost per task (USD)\",\n       \"accTitle\": \"How to Read This Chart\",\n       \"notes\": [\n        \"Each point represents a coding-agent variant. Farther right means higher benchmark performance, while lower on the chart means lower average cost per task. The most efficient agents sit toward the lower-right: stronger results at lower cost.\"\n       ],\n       \"viewBox\": null,\n       \"kinds\": null,\n       \"tables\": 0\n      }\n     ]\n    }\n   ]\n  },\n  {\n   \"id\": \"execution-time\",\n   \"cards\": [\n    {\n     \"panels\": [\n      {\n       \"tab\": \"Execution Time\",\n       \"param\": \"?coding-agents-token-usage-chart=token-usage&coding-agents-performance-chart=index&coding-agents-harness-comparison-chart=harness-index&coding-agents-cost-chart=cost-to-run\",\n       \"h3\": \"Time per Task\",\n       \"caption\": \"Average agent wall time per task · Lower is better\",\n       \"accTitle\": \"What Execution Time Is Measuring\",\n       \"notes\": [\n        \"This chart uses agent wall time: how long the agent process was actively running on each task.\",\n        \"It does not include environment startup, verifier or judge time, or other harness overhead, so it is a cleaner comparison of how long the agent itself was working.\"\n       ],\n       \"viewBox\": null,\n       \"kinds\": null,\n       \"tables\": 0\n      },\n      {\n       \"tab\": \"Turns\",\n       \"param\": \"?coding-agents-token-usage-chart=token-usage&coding-agents-performance-chart=index&coding-agents-harness-comparison-chart=harness-index&coding-agents-cost-chart=cost-to-run&coding-agents-execution-time-chart=mean-steps\",\n       \"h3\": \"Turns per Task\",\n       \"caption\": \"Average number of agent turns per task · Lower is better\",\n       \"accTitle\": \"What Turns Is Measuring\",\n       \"notes\": [\n        \"This chart shows the average number of turns the agent takes per task. It is a rough proxy for how many actions, tool calls, and iteration cycles an agent is using to complete benchmark tasks.\"\n       ],\n       \"viewBox\": null,\n       \"kinds\": null,\n       \"tables\": 0\n      }\n     ]\n    },\n    {\n     \"tabs\": null,\n     \"panels\": [\n      {\n       \"h3\": \"Artificial Analysis Coding Agent Index vs. Execution Time\",\n       \"caption\": \"Artificial Analysis Coding Agent Index vs. average agent wall time per task\",\n       \"accTitle\": \"How to Read This Chart\",\n       \"notes\": [\n        \"Each point represents a coding-agent variant. Farther right means higher benchmark performance, while lower on the chart means shorter average agent runtime per task. Agents toward the lower-right deliver stronger results in less active agent time.\"\n       ],\n       \"viewBox\": null,\n       \"kinds\": null,\n       \"tables\": 0\n      }\n     ]\n    }\n   ]\n  }\n ]\n}"